Question

Find the highest-paid employee in each department using ROW_NUMBER()

| dept | emp_id | salary |
| ---- | ------ | ------ |
| IT   | 102    | 7000   |
| HR   | 105    | 5500   |

ROW_NUMBER() is a window function that assigns a unique sequential integer to each row within a partition of the result set.

Why it is used

It is used when you need:
a unique row index inside each partition
to rank rows by some order
to remove duplicates while keeping the first/last row
to select top-N rows per group

Common uses
Get the first row per group
Example: choose the latest order for each customer
Deduplicate rows
Keep only rows where ROW_NUMBER = 1 after ordering
Pagination or ranking
Number rows in a sorted result for reporting or filtering
Top-N per partition
Find top 3 products by sales per category

| emp_id | name  | salary | ROW_NUMBER | RANK | DENSE_RANK |
| ------ | ----- | ------ | ---------- | ---- | ---------- |
| 101    | John  | 10000  | 1          | 1    | 1          |
| 102    | Mike  | 9000   | 2          | 2    | 2          |
| 103    | Sara  | 9000   | 3          | 2    | 2          |
| 104    | David | 8000   | 4          | 4    | 3          |
| 105    | Emma  | 7000   | 5          | 5    | 4          |
 """

#SQL

select 
    dept, emp_id, salary, 
    row_number() over (partition by dept order by salary desc) as rn
from Emp
where rn =1;


#pyspark
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.window import Window 
from pyspark.sql.functions import row_number, col


spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("RowNumberExample").getOrCreate()  

data = [
    (101, 'IT', 5000),
    (102, 'IT', 7000),
    (103, 'IT', 6000),
    (104, 'HR', 4000),
    (105, 'HR', 5500)]

columns = ['emp_id', 'dept', 'salary']

df =spark.createDataFrame(data, columns)

res_df = df.withColumn("rn",row_number().over (Window.partitionBy("dept").orderBy(col("salary").desc())))
res_df.filterCol(("rn")==1).select("dept","emp_id","salary").show()
